= [+ year_display +] [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] Conference

The transformation of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] into an interfaith party is now set in stone, but Sedgewick has made himself some enemies in doing so. Conservative Faithful have jumped ship [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": to the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>.?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": to the various right-wing parties that claim to have Faithful interests at heart.?] The left of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] under Joseph Werth has become a thorn in Sedgewick's side due to his antipathy towards the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>.

The reformation of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] away from its religious roots has injected a dose of <span class="tooltip-text" title="good mod">dynamism</span> into the party, making it more willing to change and evolve with current conditions. Aldwin Stilling is a rising star on the left, <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> wing of the party, supporting Sedgewick's vision for a united Faithful guild but disagreeing with his right-wing policies. 

- @stegerwald: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] elects Adam Sedgewick as the party chair.
- @kaiser: Influence the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] to select Aldwin Stilling as the party chair.
- @kaiser_campaign: We will hold a campaign in support of Aldwin Stilling as party chair.

@stegerwald
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 6; unionist_ideology = "Right"; stegerwald_skibidi_time = time + 11
face-image: img/portraits/stegerwald.jpg

Sedgewick will continue to evolve the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] into a <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span>, <span style="color: #586593;">democratic</span>, <span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth</span>, and <span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> party. Hopefully, Joseph Werth and the left wing of the party will be able to keep him in check. [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": However, the party will continue shifting to the right as it takes the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s place on the Commonwealth right. ?]

[? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": Talks of a merger with the <span style='color: #3E88B3;'>**Traditionalists**</span> are becoming increasingly common—though support is limited to their <span style='color: #0087DC;'>People's Conservatives</span> and <span style='color: #6D5298;'>Faithful Socials</span>. A merger remains impossible without one of those factions having strong, centralized leadership within their party. At the same time, we must prevent any government cooperation between them and the <span style='color: #000000;'>Unionists</span>—lest we allow conditions for such a union to emerge. ?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": A merger with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> is out of the question—at least with Mallin commanding the party. Still, there remains fertile ground on the anti-Mallin right. ?]

@kaiser
choose-if: unionist_relation >= 70 and pro_republic >= 75
unavailable-subtitle: [? if unionist_relation < 70 : Our relations are not high enough. ?] [? if pro_republic < 75 : The party isn't left-wing enough for someone like him. ?]
on-arrival: unionist_relation += 10; unionist_ideology = "Left"; unionist_leader = "Stilling"; liberal_cooperation += 2; commons_unionist += 5; commons_marcher -= 5; disfavored_unionist += 5; landed_unionist -= 4; guild_unionist -= 8; landed_traditionalist += 4 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_traditionalist += 8 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; faithful_traditionalist += 4 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; landed_kvp += 4 if kvp_formed; guild_kvp += 8 if kvp_formed; faithful_kvp += 4 if kvp_formed; landed_other += 4 if not kvp_formed and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; guild_other += 8 if not kvp_formed and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; faithful_other += 4 if not kvp_formed and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; heartland_leader = "Sedgewick" if heartland_leader == "Askew"; kaiser_time = time + 11
face-image: img/portraits/kaiser.jpg

With our grassroots connections, we are able to secure the election of Aldwin Stilling to the chairmanship of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. This has come as a complete shock to the political landscape, which has been shifting to the right recently. His progressive, left-wing views on contentious subjects like nationalizations and his vehement anti-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">Imperial Sovereigntism</span> are ahead of his time. 

Despite this victory, he finds himself at odds with the rest of his party, as his views are out of place. [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": Furthermore, this has stopped the flow of <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> moderates to the party, whose voters will head back to the [? if not kvp_formed: various smaller parties between the two parties?][? if kvp_formed: the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?]. ?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": Furthermore, this has stopped the process of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] taking over the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> of being the party of the right. ?] Due to the party's <span class="tooltip-text" title="good mod">dynamism</span>, he may be deposed if he proves to be too divisive.

