With our grassroots connections, as well as a professional campaign, we are able to secure the election of Aldwin Stilling to the chairmanship of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. This has come as a complete shock to the political landscape, which has been shifting to the right recently. His progressive, left-wing views on contentious subjects like nationalizations and his vehement anti-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">Imperial Sovereigntism</span> are ahead of his time. 

Despite this victory, he finds himself at odds with the rest of his party, as his views are out of place. [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": Furthermore, this has stopped the flow of <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> moderates to the party, whose voters will head back to the various smaller parties between the two parties. ?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": Furthermore, this has stopped the process of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] taking over the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> of being the party of the right. ?] Due to the party's <span class="tooltip-text" title="good mod">dynamism</span>, he may be deposed if he proves to be too divisive.